.TH WLANLOGIN 1 2026-11-26 wlanlogin "User Commands"
.SH NAME
wlanlogin \- automatic login for the Student_CX campus Wi\-Fi portal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wlanlogin
.RB [ \-\-user | \-\-system ]
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B wlanlogin
.BR \-\-help " | " \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wlanlogin
signs in to the Student_CX captive portal and keeps the session online.
Authentication is submitted only while the computer is connected to the
Student_CX Wi\-Fi network; elsewhere, credentials can be saved in advance.
.PP
.B service install
registers a systemd service that follows Wi\-Fi changes reported by
NetworkManager, signs in automatically and checks the session periodically.
Every command accepts
.BR \-\-help .
.SH SCOPES
Installations, configuration and credentials are kept separately for two
scopes.
The scope options may appear before or after the command.
Uninstall the service of one scope before switching to the other.
.TP
.B \-\-user
The current user.
The service starts when the user logs in, and credentials are stored in the
Secret Service (GNOME Keyring, KWallet and similar).
This is the default for ordinary users.
.TP
.B \-\-system
The whole machine.
The service starts at boot, credentials are encrypted with
.BR systemd\-creds (1),
and root privileges are required.
This is the default when run as root, for example through
.BR sudo (8).
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BR login " [\fIcredential options\fR]"
Sign in with the saved credentials.
A terminal form opens when credentials are missing.
When the computer is not connected to Student_CX, the credentials are only
saved.
A manual login resumes automatic login that was paused by
.BR logout .
.TP
.BR logout " [" \-\-forget ]
Sign out of the current session and pause automatic login for the current
connection, also across service restarts.
It resumes after a manual
.B login
in the same scope or after reconnecting to the Wi\-Fi network.
.B \-\-forget
also deletes the saved credentials of the scope, even when offline or when
the portal request fails.
.TP
.BR "service install" " [\fIcredential options\fR]"
Save credentials (required on first installation), install a private copy of
the program as the background executable, then register and start the
systemd unit.
Run it again after upgrading
.B wlanlogin
to update the background copy.
.TP
.BR "service uninstall" " [" \-\-purge ]
Stop and remove the service, keeping the saved credentials.
.B \-\-purge
also removes the logs, configuration, runtime files and credentials of the
scope.
.TP
.BR "service start" ", " "service stop" ", " "service restart"
Start, stop or restart the installed service.
.B stop
keeps the installation and the automatic start.
.TP
.B service status
Show whether the service is installed, registered and running, and which
version is installed.
.TP
.BR "service logs" " [" \-n " \fIlines\fR] [" \-f ]
Show the service log.
.B \-n
sets the number of recent lines (default 100; 0 shows no history);
.B \-f
follows new entries until interrupted with Ctrl+C.
.TP
.BR "service session\-ready" ", " "service session\-end"
User scope only.
For desktops that do not reach the standard graphical session target,
.B session\-ready
synchronizes the D\-Bus activation environment once the graphical session is
ready, and
.B session\-end
withdraws that notice before logging out.
.TP
.BR "config get " \fIname\fR ", " "config set " "\fIname value\fR"
Read or save a configuration value of the scope.
.TP
.BR "config remove " \fIname\fR ", " "config list"
Restore the default value, or list all values.
The only key is
.BR log.level :
.B info
(default) logs failed portal requests;
.B debug
logs every portal request and response with credentials, cookies and device
identifiers redacted.
Restart the service to apply the change.
.TP
.BR "permission list" ", " "permission check " "[\fIid\fR], " "permission get " \fIid\fR
List, check or request platform permissions; each accepts
.BR \-\-json .
Linux defines no permissions, so the list is empty.
.TP
.B daemon
Run the automatic login loop in the foreground of the current process.
.SH CREDENTIAL OPTIONS
Accepted by
.B login
and
.BR "service install" .
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-username " \fIusername\fR"
Campus network account.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-password " \fIpassword\fR"
Password.
It is visible in the process list and shell history; prefer
.BR \-\-password\-stdin .
.TP
.B \-\-password\-stdin
Read one line from standard input as the password.
Cannot be combined with
.BR \-p .
.TP
.BR \-\-line " \fBfree1\fR|\fBfree2\fR|\fBcampus\fR"
Portal line: free line 1, free line 2, or campus intranet.
.TP
.B \-\-remember\-me
Save the account and password in the credential store of the scope (when not
connected to Student_CX, credentials are saved without authenticating).
.TP
.B \-\-interactive
Open the terminal form even when credentials are saved, to change the
account, password or line.
.TP
.B \-\-non\-interactive
Fail instead of opening the terminal form when information is missing.
.TP
.BR \-\-credential\-store " \fBnative\fR|\fBprotected\-file\fR"
System scope credential store.
.B native
uses systemd\-creds;
.B protected\-file
stores the account and password in plain text in a file readable only by
root, for older systems without systemd\-creds.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B WLANLOGIN_USERNAME
Default for
.BR \-\-username .
.TP
.B WLANLOGIN_PASSWORD
Default for
.BR \-\-password .
.TP
.B WLANLOGIN_LINE
Default for
.BR \-\-line .
.TP
.B RUST_LOG
Overrides the log filter of a foreground run, for example
.BR RUST_LOG=wlanlogin::portal::page_config=debug .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/SEUCXCS/wlanlogin/
User scope configuration
.RI ( config.json ),
line preference
.RI ( preferences.json ),
service log
.RI ( daemon.log )
and runtime files.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/SEUCXCS/wlanlogin/bin/wlanlogin\-daemon
User scope background executable.
.TP
.I /var/lib/SEUCXCS/wlanlogin/
System scope configuration, line preference and service log.
.TP
.I /run/SEUCXCS/wlanlogin/
System scope runtime files.
.TP
.I /etc/SEUCXCS/wlanlogin/
System scope credentials.
.TP
.I /usr/local/libexec/SEUCXCS/wlanlogin/wlanlogin\-daemon
System scope background executable.
.TP
.I dev.cxcs.tools.wlanlogin.service
Name of the systemd unit in both scopes.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
The command failed; the reason is printed on standard error.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid command line.
.SH EXAMPLES
Install the user service and check it:
.PP
.RS
.EX
wlanlogin \-\-user service install
wlanlogin \-\-user service status
.EE
.RE
.PP
Install the system service:
.PP
.RS
.EX
sudo wlanlogin \-\-system service install
.EE
.RE
.PP
Sign in from a script without exposing the password:
.PP
.RS
.EX
printf \(aq%s\en\(aq "$PASSWORD" | wlanlogin login \-u 2026000000 \e
    \-\-password\-stdin \-\-line free1 \-\-non\-interactive
.EE
.RE
.PP
Switch account or line:
.PP
.RS
.EX
wlanlogin logout
wlanlogin login \-\-interactive \-\-remember\-me
.EE
.RE
.PP
Collect portal diagnostics:
.PP
.RS
.EX
wlanlogin \-\-user config set log.level debug
wlanlogin \-\-user service restart
wlanlogin \-\-user service logs \-f
.EE
.RE
.SH NOTES
Software packages install only the command.
After upgrading the package, run
.B service install
again in each scope that has a service; before removing the package, run
.B service uninstall
in that scope.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR systemd\-creds (1),
.BR NetworkManager (8)
.PP
https://github.com/SEUCXCS/wlan\-auto\-login
